<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thoros of Edessa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1098">1098</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thoros was the Armenian ruler of Edessa in the late 11th century, a former Byzantine official who held the city after Byzantine power in the region collapsed. In 1098 he invited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baldwin-i-of-jerusalem">Baldwin of Boulogne</a> to help defend it and adopted him as son and heir. Weeks later Thoros was killed in a riot, and Baldwin founded the County of Edessa, the first crusader state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thoros-of-edessa.jpg" alt="Thoros of Edessa" width="320" height="488" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joseph-Nicolas Robert-Fleury · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baldwin_of_Boulogne_entering_Edessa_in_Feb_1098.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
